# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Everything here is NEXT_PUBLIC_, meaning it is
# compiled into the browser bundle: never put a secret in this file.

# Absolute base URL of this deployment. Feeds canonicals, hreflang, OG tags and
# the sitemap, so a preview must not inherit production's value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.welock.in

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostHog: optional. Both are overrides.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live project key and region are baked into
# src/components/analytics/PostHogProvider.tsx, so a normal deploy needs nothing
# here. Analytics run in production builds only; `npm run dev` never reports.
#
# Set these to point a deployment at a different PostHog project: a staging
# project, say. Set either to an EMPTY string to switch analytics off entirely
# for that deployment.
#
# KEY is the PROJECT key, the one starting `phc_`:
#   PostHog -> Settings -> Project -> Project API key
# It is public by design and belongs in the browser. The other key PostHog
# shows you, `phx_...`, is a PERSONAL key: it is a secret, it grants access to
# your whole account, and it must never appear in this file.
#
# HOST must match the region the project lives in. Point it at the wrong one
# and PostHog does not fail loudly, it just silently records nothing:
#   US -> https://us.i.posthog.com   <- this project
#   EU -> https://eu.i.posthog.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_HOST=
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID is also set in Vercel. Nothing reads it:
# posthog-js has no use for a project id; it belongs to the REST API and MCP.
